tests:
`python3 -m pytest -q tests/python/test_patch_q3-ta-menus.py`: 40 passed with the share mounted (the builder had 29; I added 11).

With the library pointed at a nonexistent directory (a scratch copy of the test file): 36 passed and 4 skipped. Each skip reads "SHARE NOT MOUNTED (...) - the staged-original, anchor, output-md5 and stock-menu validator checks did NOT run".

The suite's tests/pytest.ini (python_files = test_*.py, testpaths = python) collects the hyphenated file, so it runs under tests/run_all.sh.

The 11 new tests:
- Load order matches the engine's upper-cased comparison ("zz_menus.pk3" now sorts after "zza.pk3", which the old model got backwards).
- `--publish` against a fake share (MNT in tmp_path, `_put` stubbed; the real sharewrite.py is never called):
  - a new file is a single put, and a rerun is a no-op;
  - a different share copy is backed up to originals-2026-09-29 first, and the backup holds the bytes being replaced;
  - an existing backup is never overwritten;
  - a failed backup stops before the replacement;
  - it refuses when the title is not visible, when the manifest is stale or `--check` fails, and when the local pk3 changed after `--build`;
  - `--dry-run` writes nothing and says so;
  - the share copy is found case-insensitively.
- `--install-server`: refuses when the server directory is missing; a dry run writes nothing; a real install lands md5-verified with no .tmp left behind; a rerun skips.

I also ran `apply.py --check`, including the full 351 MB md5: exit 0. After my edits, two `--build` runs into scratch gave pk3s byte-identical to the builder's (627013444d74562c7ed28ed9caa895f2). The manifest was identical apart from local_path, and the diffs were unchanged.
